  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Counter-Trafficking Training and Technical Assistance (T&amp;TA): A Global Rapid Response Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM delivers short-term training and technical assistance (T&amp;TA) that address governments&#x2019; capacity-building needs and aims to improve the effectiveness of government responses to all forms of trafficking in persons. Beneficiaries of T&amp;TA may include host government agencies, criminal justice practitioners, and/or NGOs that are essential for creating a comprehensive anti-trafficking strategy and victim assistance network. IOM has particular expertise in victim assistance and protection, and works in collaboration with anti-trafficking experts at the country level, IOM Missions around the world, and relevant US Embassies.</narrative>
  </description>
